    "done_when": "A new tests/test_a_truncated_state_lifts_its_wait.py shows, in both the sweep reader in reckon/crew/resumption.py and the classifier reader in reckon/crew/recovery_wait.py: a probe printing OUT_OF_ME+ lifts a wait whose terminal list names OUT_OF_MEMORY; a probe printing OUT_OF_MEMORY in full still lifts it; a truncated token that is a prefix of no terminal value, such as RUNNIN+ against COMPLETED, does not lift it; and an untruncated COMPLETE does not lift a wait on COMPLETED, because only a trailing + licenses the prefix match. The test files importing each changed module add no failures against the base revision; ruff check and ruff format --check pass on the changed paths. The coordinator runs the full importer arms.",
